  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Free time",
   "texto": [
    "**Os tempos livres** is «free time». **O que gostas de fazer nos tempos livres?** = what do you like to do in your free time?",
    "Remember that «gostar» also carries **de** with verbs: gust **de** ler (read), **de** ouvir music (listen to music), **de** passear, **de** travel, **de** dançar (dance).",
    "As in Spanish, sports are «Play» (**jogar** futebol) and instruments are «They play» (**tocar** guitar)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "I'm doing: «estar a» + infinitive",
   "texto": [
    "In Portugal's standard Portuguese it is very common to express an ongoing action with **estar a + infinitivo**: **Estou a ler** = I am reading. **Está a chover** = is raining.",
    "**O que estás a fazer?** = what are you doing? The gerunde is also heard in some varieties of Portugal; it is not correct to say that it is never used there. In Brazil, gerundio is the most common form."
   ]
  },
